1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,880
Hi, in this video we'll use BURP to test horizontal access controls.

2
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:15,560
When a user logs into an application, they usually only have access to their own functions

3
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:16,560
and resources.

4
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:22,700
If access controls are incorrectly set, a user can gain access to data and functionality

5
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:25,720
that should only be available to other users.

6
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:30,540
If you have credentials for two different user accounts with identical privileges, you can

7
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:34,340
test an application's horizontal access controls.

8
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:39,420
If you want to test individual endpoints, you can use BURP Repeater.

9
00:00:39,420 --> 00:00:45,340
You can also use the Compare Sitemaps function to automatically send multiple requests.

10
00:00:45,340 --> 00:00:49,920
If you'd like to follow along, you can use the Using Application Functionality to Exploit

11
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:54,720
Insecure Deserialization Lab from our Web Security Academy.

12
00:00:54,720 --> 00:01:01,340
Before you start, make sure you have the credentials for two different users with identical privileges.

13
00:01:01,340 --> 00:01:07,680
To run a quick test on an individual endpoint, visit the target site, log in, and access the

14
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:12,440
functionality you want to test.

15
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:23,840
Then, log in with the second set of credentials that have identical privileges.

16
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:30,760
Now we'll go to the Proxy, HTTP History tab, and find a request from the first user's authenticated

17
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:33,000
session.

18
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,240
Right-click, and choose Send to Repeater.

19
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:43,500
Before we leave the HTTP History tab, we'll find the second user's most recent request, select

20
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:46,320
the request, and copy the session cookie.

21
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:49,560
Now, go to the Repeater tab.

22
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:57,260
Paste the second user's cookie into the request, replacing the original session cookie.

23
00:01:57,260 --> 00:02:00,200
Click Send.

24
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:04,500
Review the response to identify if horizontal access is possible.

25
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:08,700
In the example, the account details automatically update.

26
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:13,780
This indicates that you can't access the first user's account page using the second user's

27
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:14,980
session.

28
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:18,980
To do this for all requests across the site can be time-consuming.

29
00:02:18,980 --> 00:02:24,380
Burp Suite can help you automate this process across all requests in the current site map.

30
00:02:24,380 --> 00:02:28,180
First, log in and map the application.

31
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:30,260
In this case, we've already done this step.

32
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:35,140
In a new browser window, log in to the target site with a second set of credentials that have

33
00:02:35,140 --> 00:02:40,640
identical privileges to obtain a session cookie for the second user.

34
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:44,720
Go to the Proxy, HTTP History tab.

35
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:51,020
Select the second user's most recent request and copy the session cookie to use later.

36
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:55,840
Now we can create a session handling rule that adds the second user's session cookie to

37
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:58,940
all requests sent from the target tool.

38
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:04,480
From the Settings dialog, go to Sessions, Session Handling Rules and click Add.

39
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:09,020
Go to the Scope tab.

40
00:03:09,020 --> 00:03:14,180
Under Tools Scope, select Target and deselect all other tools.

41
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:24,280
Under URL Scope, select Use Custom Scope, click Add and enter the URL of the target site.

42
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:27,860
Now go back to the Details tab to define the rule.

43
00:03:27,860 --> 00:03:30,740
Under Rule Actions, click Add.

44
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:35,740
Then select Set a specific cookie or parameter value.

45
00:03:35,740 --> 00:03:37,900
Add the name of the cookie.

46
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:42,900
And set the value to the cookie you copied from your second user's request.

47
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:45,740
Keep clicking on OK to close all the open dialogs.

48
00:03:45,740 --> 00:03:51,620
You'll then see the rule added to the list of session handling rules.

49
00:03:51,620 --> 00:03:53,620
Go to the Target Sitemap tab.

50
00:03:53,620 --> 00:03:57,620
Right click the target host.

51
00:03:57,620 --> 00:03:59,620
Then select Compare Sitemaps.

52
00:03:59,620 --> 00:04:02,620
Select Use Current Sitemap.

53
00:04:02,620 --> 00:04:03,620
Then click Next.

54
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:07,500
Select Use Only Selected Branches.

55
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:09,500
And click Next.

56
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:14,500
Then select Request Map 1 again in a different session context.

57
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:18,500
Keep the default settings for each of the remaining steps.

58
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:23,500
Review the two sitemaps.

59
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:25,500
Any differences are highlighted.

60
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:29,740
Look for logged in requests that are identical.

61
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:34,380
This may indicate that you access the first user's account using the second user's session.

